From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:55:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AMLCodec: don't hang when moving on to the next file

CVideoPlayerVideo drains in a loop that neither waits nor reads its own message
queue, and takes VC_NONE as "ask again". While draining, the VC_EOF arm waits on
a data_len that never reaches zero, so the video thread never gets back to its
queue and the stream change for the next file is never read.

End the drain when the hardware has produced nothing for the decoder timeout the
next arm already uses.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp
index c3fbd94387cc8ca81207316ddd0f5f71cceac28d..5a0126f09bf42402b46a379ff100c03250a3a68a 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp
@@ -2961,8 +2961,16 @@ CDVDVideoCodec::VCReturn CAMLCodec::GetPicture(VideoPicture *pVideoPicture)
 
     return CDVDVideoCodec::VC_PICTURE;
   }
-  else if (m_drain && m_buffer_level_ready && data_len == 0)
+  // the caller's drain loop neither waits nor reads its message queue
+  else if (m_drain && m_buffer_level_ready &&
+           (data_len == 0 || elapsed_since_last_frame > std::chrono::seconds(m_decoder_timeout)))
+  {
+    if (data_len)
+      CLog::Log(LOGWARNING, "CAMLCodec::GetPicture: drain stalled, {:d} bytes left after {:d}ms",
+        data_len, elapsed_since_last_frame.count());
+
     return CDVDVideoCodec::VC_EOF;
+  }
   else if ((m_drain && m_buffer_level_ready) || (buffer_level > (streambuffer ? 100.0f : 10.0f)))
     return CDVDVideoCodec::VC_NONE;
   else if (ret != EAGAIN || elapsed_since_last_frame > std::chrono::seconds(m_decoder_timeout))
